<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Rune DSL stats demo - BUILD section, PLUS (fork) leg (CONTRACTS section 7E).

  The point of this file is how BORING it is next to build-legacy/pom.xml.
  Same corpus, same rosetta-config.yml, same `generate` goal bound to the same
  phase, same <languages>/<outputConfigurations> block, same setup class name.
  What changes is the plugin coordinate and the output directory - that is the
  drop-in story, stated as a diff:

    -  <groupId>com.regnosys.rosetta</groupId>
    -  <artifactId>rosetta-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    -  <version>9.83.0</version>
    +  <groupId>org.finos.rune</groupId>
    +  <artifactId>rune-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    +  <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>

  ====================================================================
  PARAMETER SURFACE - READ FROM THE FORK'S OWN SOURCE
  ====================================================================
  rune-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/regnosys/rosetta/maven/
    RuneGenerateMojo.java          @Mojo(name="generate",
                                         defaultPhase=GENERATE_SOURCES,
                                         requiresDependencyResolution=COMPILE,
                                         threadSafe=true)
                                   classpathElements  READ-ONLY ${project.compileClasspathElements}
                                   sourceRoots        required  ${project.compileSourceRoots}
    AbstractRuneGeneratorMojo.java languages, classPathLookupFilter, rosettaConfig,
                                   addOutputDirectoriesToCompileSourceRoots (true),
                                   failOnValidationError (true)
                                   + the accepted-and-IGNORED Xtext knobs:
                                     incrementalXtextBuild, clusteringConfig,
                                     compilerSourceLevel, compilerTargetLevel,
                                     compilerSkipAnnotationProcessing,
                                     compilerPreserveInformationAboutFormalParameters,
                                     javaSourceRoots, tmpClassDirectory,
                                     writeClasspathConfiguration,
                                     classpathConfigurationLocation,
                                     writeStorageResources
    Language.java                  <setup> / <outputConfigurations> / <javaSupport>
    OutputConfiguration.java       <name> (default DEFAULT_OUTPUT) / <outputDirectory>

  That list is a deliberate clone of the released 9.83.0 descriptor - the same
  names and defaults this demo verified independently by unzipping
  rosetta-maven-plugin-9.83.0.jar -> META-INF/maven/plugin.xml (transcribed in
  build-legacy/pom.xml's header). The fork requires EXACTLY ONE
  outputConfiguration carrying an outputDirectory
  (AbstractRuneGeneratorMojo.java:114-120) and rejects any <setup> other than
  com.regnosys.rosetta.RosettaStandaloneSetup (Language.java:29,
  AbstractRuneGeneratorMojo.java:188-193).

  ====================================================================
  classPathLookupFilter: REQUIRED HERE (unlike the legacy leg)
  ====================================================================
  RunePluginRunner.java:178-183 returns an EMPTY library-model list when the
  filter is null or blank:

      private List<RModel> parseClasspathModels() throws IOException {
          List<RModel> models = new ArrayList<>();
          if (classPathLookupFilter == null || classPathLookupFilter.isBlank()) {
              return models;
          }
          Pattern filter = Pattern.compile(classPathLookupFilter);

  That is the inverse of Xtext's "unset means scan everything", so the filter is
  NOT optional on this leg: omit it and the two builtin models never load, and
  every `string` / `metadata` reference in the corpus fails to link.

  The value below is the CDM 6.20.6 / DRR 6.34.1 consumer regex character for
  character - deliberately, to show the fork honouring the real consumer value
  unchanged. It is version-agnostic and matches the fork jar in the hermetic
  repo, which the runner full-matches against the raw classpath element string:
    ...\demo\work\.m2\org\finos\rune\rune-runtime\0.0.1-SNAPSHOT\rune-runtime-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar
    .*org[\\/]finos[\\/]rune[\\/]rune-runtime.*\.jar            -> matches
  ([\\/] is a character class of backslash-or-slash, so the Windows path form is
  covered; RunePluginRunner uses Matcher.matches(), i.e. a full match, and the
  leading `.*` absorbs the repo prefix.)

  ====================================================================
  BUILTINS: demo/corpus/builtins is NOT a source root here either
  ====================================================================
  Verified in the hermetic repo: org/finos/rune/rune-runtime/0.0.1-SNAPSHOT/
  rune-runtime-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar carries model/annotations.rosetta (2012 bytes)
  and model/basictypes.rosetta (1891 bytes) - the same two models the 9.83.0
  runtime jar carries for the legacy leg. Declaring the runtime as a project
  dependency below puts it on ${project.compileClasspathElements}, which is the
  list the runner scans. Adding demo/corpus/builtins as a fourth <sourceRoot>
  as well would declare namespace com.rosetta.model twice.

  Either way they are never GENERATED: GeneratorModel.IGNORED_FILES
  (rune-java-generator/.../generator/java/GeneratorModel.java:94-98) skips
  basictypes.rosetta and annotations.rosetta by file name inside shouldGenerate()
  (:795-797), before the namespace filter is consulted. That is what makes the
  two legs' output trees comparable at all - see demo/build/diff-trees.ps1.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>org.finos.rune.demo</groupId>
    <artifactId>demo-build-plus</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    <name>Rune DSL stats demo - Build (rune-dsl-plus fork toolchain)</name>

    <properties>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <!-- Never compile: the demo runs `generate-sources` only. -->
        <maven.main.skip>true</maven.main.skip>
        <maven.test.skip>true</maven.test.skip>
        <maven.build.cache.skip>true</maven.build.cache.skip>
        <maven.build.cache.enabled>false</maven.build.cache.enabled>

        <!-- ABSOLUTE, for the same reason as the legacy leg: the runner does
             Path.of(root) + Files.isDirectory(root) (RunePluginRunner.java:134-144)
             and Path.of(rosettaConfig) + Files.isRegularFile
             (AbstractRuneGeneratorMojo.java:197-206), so a CWD-relative value
             breaks under `mvn -f`. The output directory is resolved as
             basedir.resolve(configured).normalize() (:129-130), and resolve()
             returns an absolute argument unchanged. -->
        <demo.corpus>${project.basedir}/../../corpus</demo.corpus>
        <demo.out>${project.basedir}/../../work/build-plus-out</demo.out>
        <demo.rosettaConfig>${project.basedir}/../rosetta-config.yml</demo.rosettaConfig>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- Present ONLY to put the builtins carrier on the project compile
             classpath, which is the list classPathLookupFilter is matched
             against. Nothing here is compiled against. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.finos.rune</groupId>
            <artifactId>rune-runtime</artifactId>
            <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.finos.rune</groupId>
                <artifactId>rune-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>generate-demo-corpus</id>
                        <phase>generate-sources</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>generate</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <rosettaConfig>${demo.rosettaConfig}</rosettaConfig>

                            <sourceRoots>
                                <sourceRoot>${demo.corpus}/cdm-5.38.0</sourceRoot>
                                <sourceRoot>${demo.corpus}/iso20022-1.38.0</sourceRoot>
                                <sourceRoot>${demo.corpus}/drr-6.34.1</sourceRoot>
                            </sourceRoots>

                            <!-- The CDM/DRR consumer value, unchanged. Mandatory on
                                 this leg - see the header. -->
                            <classPathLookupFilter>.*org[\\/]finos[\\/]rune[\\/]rune-runtime.*\.jar</classPathLookupFilter>

                            <!-- Accepted and ignored by the fork (no Xtext build
                                 machinery); carried so both poms read identically. -->
                            <incrementalXtextBuild>false</incrementalXtextBuild>

                            <languages>
                                <language>
                                    <setup>com.regnosys.rosetta.RosettaStandaloneSetup</setup>
                                    <outputConfigurations>
                                        <outputConfiguration>
                                            <outputDirectory>${demo.out}</outputDirectory>
                                        </outputConfiguration>
                                    </outputConfigurations>
                                </language>
                            </languages>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
